      "id": "route-unreferenced",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "GET /index.php/apps/google_synchronization/sync-calendar  google_synchronization.googleapi.registersynccalendar  appinfo/routes.php:12 routes",
        "GET /index.php/apps/google_synchronization/sync-contacts  google_synchronization.googleapi.registersynccontacts  appinfo/routes.php:12 routes",
        "GET /index.php/apps/google_synchronization/unsync-contacts  google_synchronization.googleapi.unregistersynccontacts  appinfo/routes.php:12 routes"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "Nothing in the app calls 3 routes outside OCS. Looked for: a route name or a path in the PHP source and the templates, in 8 files of the frontend source and in the navigation of info.xml. A route stays behind when the frontend stops calling it. A route that only a client outside the app calls shows here as well, unless its method allows requests from other origins (CORS).",
        "  GET /index.php/apps/google_synchronization/sync-calendar  google_synchronization.googleapi.registersynccalendar  appinfo/routes.php:12 routes",
        "  GET /index.php/apps/google_synchronization/sync-contacts  google_synchronization.googleapi.registersynccontacts  appinfo/routes.php:12 routes",
        "  GET /index.php/apps/google_synchronization/unsync-contacts  google_synchronization.googleapi.unregistersynccontacts  appinfo/routes.php:12 routes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dev-tools-in-root",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "psalm/phar, friendsofphp/php-cs-fixer are in require-dev of composer.json. The manual recommends a vendor-bin/ of bamarni/composer-bin-plugin per tool, so that the dependencies of a tool cannot conflict with those of the app."
      ]
    },
